    "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/college-assistant-professor-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states-40795441-7607-4d36-9d3b-374a1ab3b141": {
      "title": "College Assistant Professor",
      "description": "College Assistant Professor - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States College Assistant Professor - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode College Assistant Professor 504154 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time Closing at: Jan 14 2027 - 23:55 MST Department Contact: Dr. Greg Armfield, (575) 646-4937, armfield@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The Department of Communication Studies at New Mexico State University seeks a College Assistant Professor. Position Details Position Title: College Assistant Professor College/Division: Arts and Sciences College Department: 330450-COMMUNICATION STUDIES Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate with qualifications. Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: College Assistant Professor of Communication Studies, college-track, nine-month position. The Department of Communication Studies seeks a colleague to teach a 4/4 load in the fall and spring semesters and engage in service and outreach. The candidate should be a Communication Studies generalist who can teach a wide variety of core and elective communication courses in person and online in an asynchronous format. This position will also teach courses in the Honors College. Faculty in this position are expected to teach a 4/4 course load of undergraduate courses in a face-to-face setting each spring and fall semester on the Las Cruces Campus, which offers courses in a traditional 16-week semester. Candidates will also have the opportunity to teach asynchronous online courses for the main campus and NMSU Global, which offers 8-week asynchronous courses. The department offers in-person and online undergraduate and graduate degrees. Candidates are also expected to engage in service and outreach. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Classification Standard Duties: Faculty in this position are responsible for teaching a 4/4 load, contributing to curriculum development, participating in service and outreach activities, and engaging in strategic initiatives aligned with the university, college, and department of Communication Studies at NMSU. Faculty are expected to contribute to the department, college, and university’s mission to advance innovation and address regional, national, and global challenges through research and education. Required Education, Experience, Certification/License, and Equivalency: Candidates must have earned an MA in Communication or Communication Studies, or a closely related field, by the time of hire (August 16, 2027). Experience: commitment to excellence in teaching engaging undergraduate courses in their area of expertise, student mentorship, and a strong commitment to service and outreach. Strong candidates will have taught traditional face-to-face 16-week semesters and have experience with 8-week asynchronous course formats. Additional Qualifications: Ability to work effectively in a collaborative and collegiate academic environment; can demonstrate a strong record of effective teaching at the collegiate level, as well as a strong desire and interest in service and outreach. Knowledge: Advanced understanding of human communication, specifically communication studies, communication general education, course development, and online course development. Skills: Ability to effectively teach a variety of communication courses and demonstrate effective teaching methods for collegiate courses in a face-to-face and asynchronous format. Abilities: Comprehension and reasoning to process complex academic theories, inductive and deductive reasoning with the capacity to draw logical conclusions, active listening and comprehension skills, problem-solving skills, and the ability to handle unexpected classroom dynamics, as well as social perceptiveness. Potential to collaborate with faculty and administrators on program and course development is a distinct advantage. Teaching and Curriculum Development: This position requires candidates to teach face-to-face and asynchronous courses in Las Cruces and develop new courses in their area of expertise. Experience with program development and program recruitment is a plus. This position will teach Introduction to Communication Honors, the Communication general education course, and an internship/practicum course for the William Conroy Honors College each semester, as well as Medical Shadowing. In addition to duties assigned to the Honors College, the candidate will teach undergraduate core and elective courses in the Department of Communication Studies that are aligned to their specialty. This position requires a generalist with broad knowledge of Communication Studies and the ability to teach Introduction to Communication every semester and potentially teach leadership courses, communication theory and practice, organizational communication, small group, persuasion, political communication, culture, deception, and interpersonal communication. Candidates with past experience working with and/or teaching honors courses as well as online asynchronous courses, online program development, and academic recruitment are preferred. This position will work with the Department Head of Communication Studies and the Associate Dean of the Honors College. Applicants should submit the following: 1) a letter of interest addressing teaching philosophy and professional goals as well as interest in working in our department, 2) a curriculum vitae, 3) evidence of teaching effectiveness in face-to-face and online environments, 4) a statement describing how the candidate’s teaching has been influenced by multicultural scholarship or diverse ways of thinking and learning; 5) contact information for three references who will be asked to submit electronic letters of reference if the candidate is chosen for an interview. All material must be submitted by January 3, 2027 at midnight Mountain Time. Please apply online at https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/search Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives – and the lives of the people they love – through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Doña Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Doña Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated “on the hill” above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 9cfe360b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 330450-COMMUNICATION STUDIES 330450-COMMUNICATION STUDIES Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) dd23030c Last Name (required) ec2f5ee9 Email (required) 300f9936 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Ext Ag/4H Agent 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 313150-ADMIN PRGM DONA ANA CTY New Mexico State University (NMSU) Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Agriculture/4-H Agent to serve Doña Ana County. This position provides educational programming and technical assistance to youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members in the areas of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Administrative Assistant Associate 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply for their Admin Assistant position. Los Alamos Extension office provides the people of New Mexico with practical, research-based knowledge and programs to improve their quality of life. The selected candidate will work fully in person in Los Alamos County, offering an excellent opportunity for direct collaboration and engagement. Assistant Professor – Artificial Intelligence Education Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE New Mexico State University invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Applied AI (9-month appointments). Faculty will join an interdisciplinary cluster hire and be affiliated with the new Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning. Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Doña Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Nursing Clinical Instructor 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Doña Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940735-DACC NURSING ASSOCIATE DEG PGM DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: College Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330450-COMMUNICATION STUDIES The Department of Communication Studies at New Mexico State University seeks a College Assistant Professor. Apply Now First Name (required) 3427