    "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/associate-vp-research-administration-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate VP Research Administration",
      "description": "Associate VP Research Administration - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Associate VP Research Administration - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Associate VP Research Administration 504184 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Oct 30 2026 - 23:55 MDT Department Contact: Stephanie Schumacher, 575-646-1590, sschum@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: Join New Mexico State University, an innovative Carnegie R1 research university, as the Associate Vice President, Research Administration. The Associate Vice President, Research Administration oversees the Research Administration department which includes central research development, pre-award and non-financial post-award administration, and research integrity and compliance. This position reports directly to the Vice President for Research, Creativity, and Economic Development (VPRCED) and serves on the VPRCED leadership team. This position manages day-to-day operations of the department, advises and actively participates in major decisions regarding university system-wide research, provides technical and regulatory direction to the VPRCED and executive university leadership, and manages department budgets. Serves as point of contact for state and federal reporting on national impacts to grant and contract opportunities and awards. Serves as institutional signature authority for all research-related funded awards and non-funded agreements. Position Details Position Title: Associate VP Research Administration College/Division: Research, Creativity and ED Department: 470300-RESEARCH ADMINISTRATION Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Not Applicable Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $165,000 Commensurate with experience and qualifications Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Contingent upon funding Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Not Applicable Job Duties and Responsibilities: The Associate Vice President, Research Administration oversees the Research Administration department which includes central research development, pre-award and non-financial post-award administration, and research integrity and compliance. This position reports directly to the Vice President for Research, Creativity, and Economic Development (VPRCED) and serves on the VPRCED leadership team. This position manages day-to-day operations of the department, advises and actively participates in major decisions regarding university system-wide research, provides technical and regulatory direction to the VPRCED and executive university leadership, and manages department budgets. Serves as point of contact for state and federal reporting on national impacts to grant and contract opportunities and awards. Serves as institutional signature authority for all research-related funded awards and non-funded agreements. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Master's degree in a related field and Six (6) years of increasingly progressive central university management experience in two (2) or more areas that report to this position: research development, pre-award and non-financial post-award administration, and research integrity and compliance. Equivalent Qualifications: Not Applicable Preferred Qualifications: Not Applicable Special Certification/Licensure: Not Applicable Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives – and the lives of the people they love – through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Doña Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Doña Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated “on the hill” above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 21d4b13b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 470300-RESEARCH ADMINISTRATION 470300-RESEARCH ADMINISTRATION Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) f9b74478 Last Name (required) 96dbf51b Email (required) 5144f590 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Ext Ag/4H Agent 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 313150-ADMIN PRGM DONA ANA CTY New Mexico State University (NMSU) Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Agriculture/4-H Agent to serve Doña Ana County. This position provides educational programming and technical assistance to youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members in the areas of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Administrative Assistant Associate 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply for their Admin Assistant position. Los Alamos Extension office provides the people of New Mexico with practical, research-based knowledge and programs to improve their quality of life. The selected candidate will work fully in person in Los Alamos County, offering an excellent opportunity for direct collaboration and engagement. Assistant Professor – Artificial Intelligence Education Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE New Mexico State University invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Applied AI (9-month appointments). Faculty will join an interdisciplinary cluster hire and be affiliated with the new Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning. Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Doña Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Nursing Clinical Instructor 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Doña Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940735-DACC NURSING ASSOCIATE DEG PGM DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: College Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330450-COMMUNICATION STUDIES The Department of Communication Studies at New Mexico State University seeks a College Assistant Professor. Apply Now First Name (required) b3558584 Last Name (required) 0b8e9f9d Email (required) 7ee486a6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalize content such as job recommendations, and to analyze our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
