    "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/fiscal-assistant-senior-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states-24f505a2-93b2-4d1b-9ec8-fc13939d9700": {
      "title": "Fiscal Assistant Senior",
      "description": "Fiscal Assistant Senior - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Fiscal Assistant Senior - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Fiscal Assistant Senior 504173 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Oct 30 2026 - 23:55 MDT Department Contact: Juanita Hannan, 505-646-3784, juamendo@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The College of HEST seeks a Senior Fiscal Assistant position. This is a 12-month full-time position requiring on-campus, in-person presence. Position Details Position Title: Fiscal Assistant Senior College/Division: College of Hlth, Educ & Soc Trans Department: 320001-COLLEGE OF HLTH, EDUC & SOC TRANS Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: $17.85 Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Non-Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: The Fiscal Assistant Senior provides direct fiscal and administrative support to principal investigators for externally funded projects and other assigned funds. The position is responsible for initiating and processing financial and personnel transactions, maintaining supporting documentation and transaction records, and assisting with routine monitoring of assigned project accounts. The position works closely with principal investigators and other Research Operations staff to facilitate timely and accurate processing of project activities. Primary Duties and Responsibilities • Serve as a primary point of contact for assigned principal investigators for routine fiscal and administrative transactions. • Initiate and process financial transactions for sponsored projects and other assigned funds, including AggieMart purchases, PCard transactions, travel reimbursements, payment forms, journal vouchers, and other fiscal transactions. • Gather and maintain appropriate supporting documentation and business purpose information for transactions prior to routing for review and approval. • Initiate personnel and hiring actions for faculty, staff, temporary employees, and students, including postings and other required employment documentation. • Initiate PAFs, EPAFs, labor redistributions, funding changes, and other personnel-related transactions. • Maintain transaction logs, supporting records, and other documentation for assigned project accounts. • Review account activity for assigned principal investigators and assist with account reconciliation in coordination with the Accountant Intermediate. • Review employee effort allocation information for assigned projects, identify potential discrepancies, and coordinate necessary follow-up for Sponsored Projects Accounting reporting. • Monitor the status of initiated transactions and follow up on outstanding or returned items. • Assist with project closeout by processing outstanding transactions and providing documentation needed for the Final Report of Expenditures and other closeout activities. • Communicate with principal investigators, departmental personnel, and Research Operations team members regarding transaction status, required documentation, and routine administrative requirements. • Assist other Research Operations team members as needed and perform other related duties as assigned. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: High School diploma + 3 years of relevant experience or an Associate's Degree + 1 year of relevant experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Microsoft Excel and experience analyzing financial data. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives – and the lives of the people they love – through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Doña Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Doña Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated “on the hill” above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 9468a518 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 320001-COLLEGE OF HLTH, EDUC & SOC TRANS 320001-COLLEGE OF HLTH, EDUC & SOC TRANS Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) bf6e2250 Last Name (required) 63ed04a5 Email (required) df8a97ce Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Ext Ag/4H Agent 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 313150-ADMIN PRGM DONA ANA CTY New Mexico State University (NMSU) Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Agriculture/4-H Agent to serve Doña Ana County. This position provides educational programming and technical assistance to youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members in the areas of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Administrative Assistant Associate 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply for their Admin Assistant position. Los Alamos Extension office provides the people of New Mexico with practical, research-based knowledge and programs to improve their quality of life. The selected candidate will work fully in person in Los Alamos County, offering an excellent opportunity for direct collabo