      "description": "College Assistant Professor - Remote Locations, New Mexico, United States College Assistant Professor - Remote Locations, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode College Assistant Professor 504144 Remote Locations, New Mexico, United States Faculty 9-Month Faculty Full-Time Closing at: Oct 23 2026 - 23:55 MDT Department Contact: Kevin Melendrez, (575) 646-4901, kdm@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The Department of Accounting and Information Systems at New Mexico State University is seeking to fill a 9-month, non-tenure track Assistant Professor position in the area of accounting. Applicants are expected to work full-time for NMSU during the contract period and fully remote candidates will be considered for the position. The position will start January 14, 2027. Travel Requirements: Occasional travel and participation in in-person events may be required to support student and program success. Location Preference: Candidates residing in New Mexico are preferred but not required. This remote position may be performed from most U.S. locations with a dedicated, distraction-free workspace and reliable high-speed internet access. Work Eligibility: This position is not eligible for employment in CA, CO, IN, NJ, NY, OH, OR, PA, WA, or MN. Position Details Position Title: College Assistant Professor College/Division: Business College Department: 340100-ACCOUNTING AND INFORMATION SYSTEMS Location: Remote Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: 87,410 Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is a bargaining unit position with the National Education Association (NEA). Contingent Upon Funding: Not Applicable Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: The position carries a course load of 12 credit hours per semester and an expectation of active participation in service duties related to the department and college. Online course delivery (asynchronous or synchronous) is required. The successful candidate will have responsibilities teaching students enrolled in the NMSU Global Campus and is expected to contribute to an educational environment that supports learning for individuals from diverse backgrounds. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Candidates for this position are required to hold a master’s or Ph.D. degree in accounting from an AACSB International accredited business school. Candidates with a master’s degree must have at least 5 years of relevant professional experience. Those with a Ph.D. must have experience that will qualify them to meet AACSB academic qualifications. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: The candidate should be able to teach undergraduate courses in accounting in an online delivery method. Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. Physical Effort: No or very limited physical effort required. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 res