    "https://careers.nmsu.edu/jobs/supervisor-lab-las-cruces-new-mexico-united-states": {
      "title": "Supervisor, Lab",
      "description": "Supervisor, Lab - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Supervisor, Lab - Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Kiosk mode Supervisor, Lab 504132 Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Staff Staff Full-time Closing at: Oct 23 2026 - 23:55 MDT Department Contact: Israel Joukhadar, 575-646-5280, icalsoya@nmsu.edu Internal or External Search: External - Open to all applicants Advertising Summary: The Plant and Environmental Sciences Department at New Mexico State University is seeking a Supervisor, Laboratory to provide technical and operational support for laboratory, greenhouse, and field research activities across multiple funded research projects. The position oversees day-to-day research operations, including equipment maintenance and troubleshooting, greenhouse and irrigation systems, laboratory instrumentation, field activities, and research site coordination. Position Details Position Title: Supervisor, Lab College/Division: Agricultural,Consumer & Env Sci Col Department: 301400-PLANT AND ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCES Location: Las Cruces Offsite Location (if applicable): Target Hourly/Salary Rate: Commensurate with qualifications. Appointment Full-time Equivalency: 1.0 FLSA Status : Exempt Bargaining Unit Announcement: This is NOT a bargaining unit position with American Federation of State, County & Municipal Employees (AFSCME). Contingent Upon Funding: Contingent upon external funding Standard Work Schedule: Standard (M-F, 8-5) If Not a Standard Work Schedule: Job Duties and Responsibilities: ****THIS IS A 3 YEAR APPOINTMENT**** Provides essential technical and operational support for research activities, including equipment maintenance, laboratory and field operations, supply management, and coordination of research-related activities across multiple funded projects. Performs preventive maintenance, calibration, troubleshooting, and repair coordination for greenhouse environmental control systems, Dosatron fertigation injectors, irrigation systems, field sensor arrays, and laboratory analytical instrumentation. Ensures equipment is properly maintained and operational to support the continuity and quality of research activities. Schedules, trains, and directs the daily work of graduate and undergraduate student employees assigned to multiple funded research projects. Provides safety, equipment, and operational training; monitors compliance with established research protocols and safety procedures; reviews and verifies timesheets; and serves as the first-line point of contact for personnel, scheduling, and day-to-day operational issues. Manages procurement, receiving, storage, and inventory of fertilizers, growing media, plant protection products, laboratory reagents, and field consumables. Maintains adequate inventory levels and coordinates the timely acquisition and distribution of supplies necessary to support ongoing research activities. Implements and documents integrated pest management rotations, fertigation programs, and irrigation schedules. Coordinates plot preparation, planting, maintenance, and harvest activities across multiple research sites. Monitors crop and plant conditions, identifies potential issues, and takes or coordinates corrective action to minimize impacts to research trials. Maintains accurate and comprehensive pesticide application, chemical inventory, safety, equipment, and research-related records. Ensures documentation and operational practices comply with applicable University policies and procedures, as well as state and federal laws and regulatory requirements. Supports required reporting, recordkeeping, and compliance activities associated with laboratory, greenhouse, and field research operations. Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Associate's Degree + 4 years of relevant experience or a Bachelor's degree + 2 years of relevant experience. Equivalent Qualifications: Preferred Qualifications: Requires knowledge of greenhouse and controlled environment and open field production, fertilizer chemistry and fertigation injector operation, integrated pest management and pesticide regulations, field plot research procedures, laboratory and chemical safety standards Special Certification/Licensure: Working Conditions and Physical Effort Environment: Work is normally performed indoors. Physical Effort: Light physical effort. Effort applies to no more than two (2) hours per day. Lifting Requirements: Requires handling of average-weight objects up to 10 pounds or some standing or walking. Risk: Work environment involves some exposure to hazards or physical risks, which require following basic safety precautions. Recruitment Summary We are New Mexico’s land-grant institution and a comprehensive research university dedicated to teaching, research public service and outreach at all levels. NMSU is a welcoming community of talented faculty, staff and students who are working together to make a difference. We are a NASA Space Grant College, a Hispanic-serving institution (HSI), a minority-serving institution (MSI) and home to the first Honors College in New Mexico. We offer an accessible education that shapes bright futures. NMSU provides learning opportunities to a diverse population of students and community members at four campuses, Cooperative Extension offices located in each of New Mexico’s 33 counties, 12 research and science centers, and through distance education. NMS U Global Campus Since 1888, NMSU has proudly embodied this tradition, building relationships that last a lifetime while serving students who want to earn their degree and grow in their field. Today, NMSU Global Campus provides flexible, career-focused online education that helps our students transform their lives – and the lives of the people they love – through over 70 degree and certificate programs, skill-building microlearning courses, and career and talent development. NMSU Main Campus Located in Las Cruces, NM, New Mexico State University's 900-acre main campus is located at the crossroads of I-10 and I-25 in the Southwestern United States. As a thriving center of higher education, deeply rooted in the regional tradition, its role as a comprehensive university is recognized throughout the state. Doña Ana Community College Founded in 1973 in collaboration with local school districts to support occupational education, DACC is now a leading community college that provides transformative educational opportunities that meet the workforce needs of Doña Ana County. With a focus on access, innovation and excellence, DACC offers over ninety degrees and certificates, adult education, specialized workforce training, and small business assistance. Alamogordo Campus Established in 1958 to serve the needs of the airmen and families stationed at Holloman Air Force Base located only 10 miles west of Alamogordo, NMSUA is a community college with a long history of excellence that is supported by a caring community of hard-working students and dedicated faculty and staff. The campus is situated “on the hill” above Alamogordo and provides inspiring views of the city and the Tularosa Basin, offering the perfect venue for creative and motivated learning. Grants Campus NMSU Grants was established as a branch of New Mexico State University in 1968 through the cooperative efforts of New Mexico State University and Grants Municipal Schools. As a two-year branch community college, NMSU Grants serves the local communities in Cibola and McKinley counties, including the Pueblos of Acoma, Laguna, and Zuni, as well as Tohajiilee, San Mateo, San Rafael, Cubero, the City of Grants, and the Village of Milan. Special Instructions to Applicants The electronic application is the *official* document that will be used to qualify applicants. Paper/email documents will not be accepted. Required documents must be attached to this application. EEO Statement New Mexico State University does not discriminate in employment on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, political affiliation, marital status, disability, genetic information, age, military service, or other non-merit factor. Requesting an Accommodation Individuals with disabilities are encouraged to apply. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and New Mexico State University policy, if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply, interview, or complete onboarding for a position with New Mexico State University, or if you cannot use the online application system, please visit our Accessibility & Accommodations page to initiate an accommodation request Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 6cf62f12 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 301400-PLANT AND ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCES 301400-PLANT AND ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCES Locations Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States First Name (required) c3aed0c6 Last Name (required) b21a18ae Email (required) a04fb35e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Ext Ag/4H Agent 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 313150-ADMIN PRGM DONA ANA CTY New Mexico State University (NMSU) Cooperative Extension Service is seeking an Extension Agriculture/4-H Agent to serve Doña Ana County. This position provides educational programming and technical assistance to youth, agricultural producers, families, and community members in the areas of agriculture, 4-H youth development, and community engagement. The successful candidate will develop, coordinate, implement, and evaluate Extension educational programs based on the needs of the local community. Administrative Assistant Associate 1780 East University Avenue, NMSU satellite location, New Mexico, United States, 88003 312050-ADMIN PRGM LOS ALAMOS CTY Los Alamos Cooperative Extension office invites you to apply for their Admin Assistant position. Los Alamos Extension office provides the people of New Mexico with practical, research-based knowledge and programs to improve their quality of life. The selected candidate will work fully in person in Los Alamos County, offering an excellent opportunity for direct collaboration and engagement. Assistant Professor – Artificial Intelligence Education Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330500-COMPUTER SCIENCE New Mexico State University invites applications for two tenure-track Assistant Professor positions in Applied AI (9-month appointments). Faculty will join an interdisciplinary cluster hire and be affiliated with the new Institute for Applied Practice in AI and Machine Learning. Instructor, Early Childhood 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Doña Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940831-DACC EARLY CHILDHOOD EDUCATION DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: Nursing Clinical Instructor 2800 Sonoma Ranch Boulevard, Doña Ana Community College, New Mexico, United States, 88011 940735-DACC NURSING ASSOCIATE DEG PGM DACC, a responsive, accessible, comprehensive, learning-centered community college that provides education opportunities to a diverse community of learners is inviting candidates to apply for the following vacant position: College Assistant Professor Las Cruces, New Mexico, United States 330450-COMMUNICATION STUDIES The Department of Communication Studies at New Mexico State University seeks a College Assistant Professor. Apply Now First Name (required) 2dc59042 Last Name (required) d02062de Email (required) 1f6d87bc Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidat